    -> Transaction Attributes in Spring
    -----------------------------------
        1. Propagation
            a. Required
                -> If any existing transaction will be there then it will join or else this will create new transaction.
            b. Required New
                -> If any existing transaction will be there then it will suspend that and it will create new one everytime.
            c. Mandatory
                -> if no transaction will be there then it will throw exceptions.
            d. Nested
                -> Inside existing transaction, here it create new transaction.
            e. Supported
                -> Executes within transaction.
            f. Not-Supported
                -> Executes without transactions.
            g. Never
                -> If transaction found then it will throw exception.
        2. Isolation
            a. READ_UNCOMMITTED
                -> Allows a transaction to read data that has been modified by other transactions but not yet committed.
            b. READ_COMMITTED
                -> Ensures that a transaction reads only committed data. It prevents dirty reads.
            c. REPEATABLE_READ
                -> Guarantees that if a transaction reads the same data twice, the data will not change during the transaction.
            d. SERIALIZABLE
                -> Highest level of isolation. Ensures that transactions are executed sequentially, as if they were run one after another.
        3. ReadOnly
            -> Used when method सिर्फ data read कर रही है
            -> @Transactional(readOnly = true)
                ✅ Performance improve
                ✅ Prevent unnecessary locks
        4. Time-Out
            -> Transaction max कितने seconds तक चलेगा
            -> @Transactional(timeout = 5)
            -> अगर time exceed हुआ तो rollback होगा
        5. Rollback
            -> @Transactional(rollbackFor = Exception.class)


